  "created": "2026-07-18T02:51:02.957Z",
  "description": "Random-access (seekable) reading of zstandard streams: reads and writes the official zstd seekable format, and builds a verified resume-point index for ordinary (non-seekable) zstd streams.",
  "id": "ZstdSeekable",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-07-18T02:53:41.043Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "YWL3xPUpa1oz4j2aDRfLJoytzaq3yGKFOfcn8ps0MSSz0927yyQpRLbJs1v34KLz43kAuntnlc7Gvhd/h/enPg==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 113288,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/fiddyschmitt/ZstdSeekable",
  "published": "2026-07-18T02:51:02.957Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Exact decoder-state resume points: each mid-frame point now snapshots the full carried zstd decoder state (entropy tables, repeat offsets, table-selector classification and flags) alongside the window, so EVERY block boundary at the target spacing is accepted - 100% boundary acceptance, no dropped candidates, no divergence fallback, and the build is a single decode pass (a small sample of spans is still byte-verified as an integration check). Interrupted builds resume from the last sealed point via exact restore (no fast-forward decode), guarded by a compressed-stream fingerprint. New ZSTZRAN4 index format (ZSTZRAN1/2/3 files still load and serve unchanged).",
